{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender editor types blender editor types","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md","fileName":"Blender Editor Types.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Editor Types","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Interface and Workflow]] · [[Blender Editor Structure]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Interface and Workflow","Blender Editor Structure","Blender SpaceLink Structure","Blender SpaceType Structure","Blender Screen Area Structure","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender editor types blender editor types","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md","fileName":"Blender Editor Types.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Editor Types","heading":"Blender Editor Types","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender can be understood as several specialized programs sharing one interface and the same underlying data. Each editor type presents a particular way to inspect or change that data, such as the 3D Viewport, Graph Editor, Shader Editor, Outliner, or Text Editor.\n\nBecause an area's editor type can be changed, a layout is not tied permanently to one task. The artist can replace an editor when the work changes while leaving the rest of the window intact.\n\nAt the core-code level, each editor instance stores persistent data through a [[Blender SpaceLink Structure]] derivative, while a [[Blender SpaceType Structure]] holds its runtime callbacks and supported regions. A [[Blender Screen Area Structure]] joins these two sides so the same visible area can retain layout state and select the behavior of its current editor type.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Interface and Workflow","Blender Editor Structure","Blender SpaceLink Structure","Blender SpaceType Structure","Blender Screen Area Structure","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender editor types blender editor types","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Editor Types.md","fileName":"Blender Editor Types.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Editor Types","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf]]\n\n[[coreblenderdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Interface and Workflow","Blender Editor Structure","Blender SpaceLink Structure","Blender SpaceType Structure","Blender Screen Area Structure","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}